1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:05,639
This is the Watterson household, and I guarantee you don't know everything about it.

2
00:00:05,860 --> 00:00:07,980
Like, tell me, do you know where this room is?

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:10,140
It works fine.

4
00:00:11,599 --> 00:00:14,300
Or better yet, where is this room in the house?

5
00:00:15,970 --> 00:00:18,280
Actually, here's just my biggest question of all.

6
00:00:18,699 --> 00:00:20,579
You've seen this shot a million times.

7
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:23,620
Tell me, where does the door behind the couch lead to?

8
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:25,559
Yeah, the brown door right there.

9
00:00:25,579 --> 00:00:26,339
I'll give you a moment.

10
00:00:29,079 --> 00:00:29,879
Can't remember, huh?

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,380
Well, there's a good reason why, and I'll fill you in on it in due time.

12
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,560
Just know, it already don't make no sense.

13
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:41,600
So today, I'm going to show you, yes you, exactly how the Watterson's household works, and how it doesn't work.

14
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:44,320
Amazing worlds don't have to make sense, you'll see.

15
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:48,759
Now, the first step to figuring out how a place like this even works is getting an idea of the

16
00:00:48,759 --> 00:00:52,600
layout, and thankfully, we actually have a pretty solid blueprint to work with here.

17
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:54,670
For now, let's just get a good look at the first floor.

18
00:00:55,039 --> 00:00:56,659
Starting off, let's take a look at the porch.

19
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,420
Well, the water's as ours.

20
00:01:01,799 --> 00:01:03,119
And if that's too cluttered for you,

21
00:01:03,219 --> 00:01:07,140
here's just a general look at what the porch looks like in a lot of establishing shots in the show.

22
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:10,780
Then we got the family room, or as I prefer to call it, the living room.

23
00:01:10,939 --> 00:01:15,359
When you're deciding where to go for a hamburger, you're a little further than the burger bar.

24
00:01:15,579 --> 00:01:20,120
There, you can see both angles pretty well.

25
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:22,620
And then attached to the living room is the dining room.

26
00:01:22,819 --> 00:01:25,140
Basically, just a dinner table in the corner of the room.

27
00:01:25,340 --> 00:01:27,340
He looks so simple on tea tree.

28
00:01:27,719 --> 00:01:30,719
I mean, while I personally would prefer a full dining room,

29
00:01:30,879 --> 00:01:34,060
at least Richard can look across the table to watch TV while eating breakfast.

30
00:01:34,319 --> 00:01:36,299
Then, of course, we have the kitchen, shown here.

31
00:01:38,359 --> 00:01:40,969
Then we have the laundry room, as we saw earlier.

32
00:01:42,879 --> 00:01:46,579
This place is weird because it's basically always shown to be there.

33
00:01:46,819 --> 00:01:50,060
Like, that door in the back of that shot is always directly connected to the kitchen,

34
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:52,319
but we really only see the inside of it once.

35
00:01:52,599 --> 00:01:54,780
But moving on, finally, we have the parents' room.

36
00:01:56,310 --> 00:01:57,680
What's going on?

37
00:01:57,900 --> 00:01:59,099
I had a nightmare.

38
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:03,719
And it's this room right here where things really start to make no sense at all.

39
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:05,859
So according to our blueprint layout of the home,

40
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:10,599
this bedroom is through that brown door in the background that we see in most shots of the living room.

41
00:02:10,879 --> 00:02:15,360
And yes, this door is pretty much always there, unmistakably existent.

42
00:02:15,479 --> 00:02:17,500
Here it is in season one's The Dress.

43
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:19,219
Come on, we're gonna be late for school.

44
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:24,240
And here it is all the way in season six's The Ad, still doing the whole existing thing.

45
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:24,879
Speak louder.

46
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:29,280
But all right, we know that door is existent throughout the entire series.

47
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:31,979
What we rarely ever see is where it leads to.

48
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:34,020
Now, of course, if the chart is to be believed,

49
00:02:34,219 --> 00:02:36,460
then you'll see the door as the way into the parents' room.

50
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:38,960
However, I have bad news for you.

51
00:02:39,099 --> 00:02:44,500
Look back at our clip of Richard and Nicole's room from earlier and pay close attention to the color of the door gumballs by.

52
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:46,219
I had a nightmare.

53
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:51,360
So the door is white and notably also opens inward, meaning from the outside,

54
00:02:51,659 --> 00:02:54,300
the door to Nicole and Richard's room should be white.

55
00:02:54,699 --> 00:02:57,139
But let's take another look at that door in the living room.

56
00:02:57,460 --> 00:02:58,960
Ah, yep, that's brown.

57
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:00,860
That ain't Nicole and Richard's bedroom.

58
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,599
Now that raises two questions.

59
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:03,960
First off, the easy one.

60
00:03:04,199 --> 00:03:06,180
What does that door lead to then?

61
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:08,620
Well, to answer that, we need to diverge a little bit.

62
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:10,639
Let's talk about the front door to the house.

63
00:03:10,780 --> 00:03:13,240
So the front of gumballs house is pretty iconic.

64
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:16,280
Like I'm pretty sure this image is burned into all of our brains forever now.

65
00:03:16,620 --> 00:03:20,139
But there is an issue with this layout when you think about it a bit longer.

66
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:22,699
See how the door is to the very far right of the place?

67
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:25,360
Doesn't look like there can be a separate room to the right of it.

68
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:29,599
Meaning that brown door we always see in the living room is maybe entirely useless?

69
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,960
I mean, it logically can't lead anywhere.

70
00:03:32,099 --> 00:03:33,219
Maybe it's just a vanity door.

71
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:35,580
Could the Wattersons have bought something from this place maybe?

72
00:03:35,719 --> 00:03:37,500
Get on down to real fake doors.

73
00:03:37,759 --> 00:03:38,719
Won't open.

74
00:03:39,039 --> 00:03:39,860
Won't open.

75
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:44,360
Well, as much as I'd enjoy seeing a gumball Rick and Morty crossover, the thing is,

76
00:03:44,539 --> 00:03:46,280
that front we're seeing is only one.

77
00:03:46,319 --> 00:03:47,759
One version of the front.

78
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,400
Take a look at this clip from the deal.

79
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:52,280
Oh, I forgot about the garden.

80
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:56,120
Besides the birthday banner, notice anything fishy about that shot?

81
00:03:56,259 --> 00:03:59,400
Yeah, the front door is now right in the center of the porch rather than the far right.

82
00:03:59,539 --> 00:04:02,680
Which means, if this is the layout we're usually dealing with, then sure,

83
00:04:02,860 --> 00:04:05,259
the brown door probably actually would lead somewhere.

84
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:07,039
With that said, I'll be honest,

85
00:04:07,199 --> 00:04:11,039
the original layout with the door to the side is what's most consistently seen in the show.

86
00:04:11,379 --> 00:04:13,900
So I think it's more canon than what we see in the deal.

87
00:04:14,060 --> 00:04:18,879
Heck, this footage of the house in real life actually shows the door is in fact on the left.

88
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,740
And well, I mean, let's be fair,

89
00:04:20,879 --> 00:04:26,259
I'm pretty sure the show just used a mirrored image of the house to make it more distinct and visually pleasing, I guess.

90
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:30,060
So yes, I still believe the door is usually on the right side of the house,

91
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:32,759
which means that brown door in the living room is still a mystery.

92
00:04:33,079 --> 00:04:35,920
So really, we have no true answer as to what that door leads to,

93
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,660
so we might as well go back to the bedroom and ask our other question.

94
00:04:38,839 --> 00:04:42,980
Secondly, if the parents' bedroom door is shown to be white and the brown door leads to nothing,

95
00:04:43,339 --> 00:04:45,779
where exactly is the parents' bedroom?

96
00:04:45,980 --> 00:04:47,860
Well, maybe the answer is the second floor.

97
00:04:48,079 --> 00:04:50,040
Let's take a look at this clip from the episode, The Poltergeist.

98
00:04:51,399 --> 00:04:52,339
Richard, what are you doing?

99
00:04:54,129 --> 00:04:56,860
We'll get into the layout of upstairs later, but for now,

100
00:04:57,079 --> 00:05:02,579
take my word that based on the kids' door being in the background means that this shot is indeed upstairs.

101
00:05:02,980 --> 00:05:04,220
So that solves it, right?

102
00:05:04,459 --> 00:05:07,459
The brown door leads nowhere and the parents' bedroom is right next to the kids.

103
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:08,980
Yep, that'll do it, case closed.

104
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:09,959
You know where this is going.

105
00:05:11,430 --> 00:05:16,500
No! So, Richard and Nicole's room is in fact behind the brown door,

106
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:19,300
even though their room has been shown to have a white door,

107
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:22,879
and even though that room makes no spatial sense at all given the front door.

108
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:27,600
Cool. Let's move away now from rooms that don't make much sense and instead look at one that was left

109
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:31,680
out of our layout, the iconic, beloved, never forgotten shed.

110
00:05:32,139 --> 00:05:34,060
Yeah, this kind of always gets overlooked.

111
00:05:34,399 --> 00:05:36,980
The Waterstones have been shown with a shed on many, many occasions,

112
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,800
like here it is in season one's The Robot.

113
00:05:42,769 --> 00:05:46,959
Then in season two's The Hero, we actually get to see what it looks like inside.

114
00:05:49,860 --> 00:05:52,420
I can't do this.

115
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:58,939
And we get an, ahem, entirely different sort of view of it in season three with the bros.

116
00:06:03,060 --> 00:06:06,839
See? Isn't that an iconic room?

117
00:06:07,259 --> 00:06:08,819
I'm starting to get why it's forgotten now.

118
00:06:08,899 --> 00:06:10,660
I'd love to forget that face Gumball made.

119
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:13,439
Luckily, it seems the shed was forgotten about in the episode The Fight.

120
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:18,240
There comes a point in every man's life where he has to stand up for himself.

121
00:06:18,839 --> 00:06:22,040
You know, normally I'd be mad about a magical shed that disappears and reappears,

122
00:06:22,139 --> 00:06:26,939
but after Gumball's advances in the shed earlier, I think I'm cool with this place being gone forever.

123
00:06:27,259 --> 00:06:29,600
If it were up to me, I'd probably burn the whole thing down.

124
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:33,819
Now, technically, there's one more room on the first floor that wasn't covered, and shockingly,

125
00:06:34,019 --> 00:06:35,920
it also doesn't make any sense at all.

126
00:06:36,180 --> 00:06:39,759
But I'm saving the best for last, so stay tuned for that one.

127
00:06:40,079 --> 00:06:44,060
So for now, let's move on up to the second floor, where things get even more illogical.

128
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:46,879
It looks like we really only have three main rooms here.

129
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:50,339
The hallway, which we got a brief look at earlier with the episode The Dress.

130
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:51,399
Be there in a second!

131
00:06:51,660 --> 00:06:55,600
These ice cubes will allow us to glide down the stairs at almost the speed of light.

132
00:06:55,839 --> 00:06:59,779
Then here's a look at the bathroom, which apparently is the only bathroom in the house.

133
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:02,569
Gumball Watterson, get out of this bathroom!

134
00:07:03,100 --> 00:07:06,160
Today's gonna be a wonderful day, cause I got in the shower first!

135
00:07:06,399 --> 00:07:09,100
I would dread sharing a bathroom with Richard Watterson.

136
00:07:09,990 --> 00:07:13,670
And of course, the children's bedroom, complete with a window to the front of the house.

137
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:17,860
Open this door, young lady!

138
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:21,379
And yeah, that room is also where things start to make zero sense.

139
00:07:21,579 --> 00:07:23,399
So, let me ask you a quick question here.

140
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:25,220
Who sleeps in the kids' bedroom?

141
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:29,439
We see Gumball and Darwin's names on the door, and there's even a bunk bed for the two of them,

142
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:33,350
but the problem is, Darwin doesn't sleep in a bed, he sleeps in a fishbowl.

143
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:42,779
And I mean, even though that looks incredibly cramped and uncomfortable, it makes sense Darwin would sleep in a fishbowl,

144
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:43,920
considering he's a fish.

145
00:07:44,420 --> 00:07:46,819
So, who sleeps in the other bunk of the bed then?

146
00:07:46,980 --> 00:07:48,279
Well, it's gotta be Anais, right?

147
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:51,560
Well, you definitely think so, but take a look at this clip from the episode The Date.

148
00:07:53,819 --> 00:07:55,740
Gumball, just get out of my room.

149
00:07:55,899 --> 00:07:56,839
Get out of my room.

150
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:58,680
So, Anais has her own room then.

151
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:01,019
Alright, given the door's stickers, that does make sense.

152
00:08:01,139 --> 00:08:01,660
I mean, come on.

153
00:08:01,779 --> 00:08:04,379
We know the doors mean nothing in this house after what happened with the parents' room.

154
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:08,139
At this point, I already know there's gotta be clips out there of Anais using that spare bunk.

155
00:08:08,259 --> 00:08:08,709
What do you mean?

156
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:11,500
Sussle Dude is supposed to give presents to everyone in Elmore.

157
00:08:11,740 --> 00:08:13,360
Yeah, that's not shocking, to be honest.

158
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:14,529
And also, to be honest,

159
00:08:14,639 --> 00:08:19,160
there's a million more instances of Anais sleeping in Gumballs and Darwin's room than having her own room.

160
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:21,220
Here's another clip of her using that bunk in the night.

161
00:08:24,220 --> 00:08:25,339
That's her in the top bunk, alright.

162
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:29,279
At the very corner of the frame, you can see the poster that's usually behind Darwin's fishbowl.

163
00:08:29,339 --> 00:08:33,600
So, I think it's fair to say that the instance of Anais having her own room was a one-off scenario.

164
00:08:33,649 --> 00:08:36,340
I can't really find much more footage of her having her own room,

165
00:08:36,340 --> 00:08:40,799
and I really doubt Nicole's single salary would be able to cover yet another room in the house.

166
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:45,620
But alright, now that we know who all sleeps in that room, let's talk about that window.

167
00:08:45,940 --> 00:08:49,820
Let's think back to that clip we saw earlier of Gumball and Darwin being locked out of their bedroom.

168
00:08:50,539 --> 00:08:52,200
Oh, what's mom gonna think?

169
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:54,000
We're in so much trouble!

170
00:08:54,460 --> 00:08:56,419
Now, you can't tell entirely from that shot,

171
00:08:56,879 --> 00:08:58,940
but this is indeed the window to the front of the house.

172
00:08:59,159 --> 00:09:01,139
Take one look at how the rest of the scene plays out,

173
00:09:01,179 --> 00:09:05,960
and you can clearly see how the pathway to the front door is in plain view behind Gumball and Darwin.

174
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:09,460
Alright, cool, the kids' room is directly located at the front of the house.

175
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:12,139
That even matches up with the way the chart from earlier puts it.

176
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:14,639
But I mean, again, that means nothing.

177
00:09:14,779 --> 00:09:17,019
The chart already lied to us about the parents' room.

178
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:21,080
And if you've got a keen eye like yours truly, you've already seen the issue with this window's placement.

179
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:23,759
Let's take another look at the way Gumball and Darwin go when they get upstairs.

180
00:09:27,149 --> 00:09:29,460
Open this door, young lady!

181
00:09:29,759 --> 00:09:32,899
Yep, they go up the stairs and to the right to get to their room.

182
00:09:33,059 --> 00:09:36,799
Which, since we know the stairs are already facing directly towards the door when you walk into the house,

183
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:41,360
that means that the window in the kids' room should really be facing to the side of the house.

184
00:09:41,700 --> 00:09:45,960
And yeah, the kids' room is definitely shown to be to the right side of the upstairs hallway pretty often.

185
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:48,590
Here's a clip of it in that place again in the episode The Flakers.

186
00:09:48,919 --> 00:09:50,539
Look out for the letters on the door in the background.

187
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:52,840
Darwin! Darwin!

188
00:09:53,039 --> 00:09:53,980
Please! Help!

189
00:09:54,139 --> 00:09:54,840
Help me!

190
00:09:55,159 --> 00:09:58,879
That clip again shows us pretty plainly that the room is definitely on the right side of the hallway.

191
00:09:59,159 --> 00:10:01,740
So then where could that front window actually be?

192
00:10:01,899 --> 00:10:04,789
Well, it could be in the attic if this clip from the mirror is to be believed.

193
00:10:07,639 --> 00:10:10,740
Dad! But that begs the question.

194
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:13,980
It's pretty undeniable that while it doesn't make any logical sense,

195
00:10:14,159 --> 00:10:16,639
the kids' room will always have a window to the front of the house.

196
00:10:16,879 --> 00:10:19,740
It shows up in basically every scene the room is in.

197
00:10:19,879 --> 00:10:22,000
For old time's sake, here it is again in the man.

198
00:10:22,159 --> 00:10:25,320
Talking. Is your grandma in?

199
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:26,559
Yeah, she'll be right down.

200
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,240
So the window is usually going to be impossibly placed in the kids' room.

201
00:10:30,460 --> 00:10:31,909
I think that's a fair canon location.

202
00:10:32,299 --> 00:10:34,779
Makes about as much sense as anything else in Elmore, I'll give it that.

203
00:10:34,980 --> 00:10:37,960
But actually, now that I think about it, what's going on with that attic?

204
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:38,679
So hang on.

205
00:10:38,799 --> 00:10:40,840
Let's get one more look at the front of the house again.

206
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:43,299
So if the window to the front of the house is in the kids' room,

207
00:10:43,519 --> 00:10:44,960
does that house look like it can have an attic?

208
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:46,960
I'd say absolutely not.

209
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:50,659
Honestly, it doesn't even look like that house could fit a second floor, but that's besides the point.

210
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:54,440
In case you wanted proof that yes, the attic doesn't outright replace the second floor,

211
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:56,659
you've already seen proof of the two areas coexisting.

212
00:10:56,899 --> 00:10:57,299
Remember this?

213
00:10:57,559 --> 00:10:58,740
Darwin! Darwin!

214
00:10:59,019 --> 00:10:59,879
Please! Help!

215
00:10:59,929 --> 00:11:04,320
Yep, there's your entryway to the attic, right above the hallway on the second floor.

216
00:11:04,539 --> 00:11:08,600
Even though this place looks like it can't fit anything close to an attic, this place shows up a lot.

217
00:11:08,860 --> 00:11:11,659
We just saw it in that clip from the mirror, but here it is again in the treasure.

218
00:11:12,009 --> 00:11:13,379
So, where do we start?

219
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:15,980
Dude, it's even got the window in the background still.

220
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:20,779
Even in that clip from the flakers, you can see the glare from the stupid impossible window.

221
00:11:21,139 --> 00:11:25,980
And the exact same place it'd be in the kids' room, which still shouldn't look out front, but come on,

222
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:26,720
you know it does.

223
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,879
How does this place manage to be so consistent yet also so alive?

224
00:11:29,899 --> 00:11:30,200
It's logical.

225
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:32,159
It makes absolutely zero sense.

226
00:11:32,519 --> 00:11:36,399
And on the topic of zero sense, there's another aspect of this attic that doesn't add up at all.

227
00:11:40,379 --> 00:11:42,200
Our chimney has been kidnapped!

228
00:11:42,419 --> 00:11:44,139
Since when do the Watterson's ever have a chimney?

229
00:11:44,639 --> 00:11:48,019
You can't see it in that establishing shot, and they don't really have a fireplace at all.

230
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:52,059
We can get a solid look at the roof of Gumball's placing the episode The Phone to double-check this,

231
00:11:52,159 --> 00:11:57,580
too. And then again at the end,

232
00:11:57,580 --> 00:12:00,960
we see the boys on the roof with yet again no chimney to be seen.

233
00:12:01,929 --> 00:12:05,320
You know, I'm glad I had the strength of character to give up that cell phone.

234
00:12:05,539 --> 00:12:09,139
We don't get a truly full view of the roof here, but from what we could see there,

235
00:12:09,259 --> 00:12:11,679
and based on where things fell apart in that clip from the treasure,

236
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:14,620
I think it's fair to say we should have been able to see if it was there.

237
00:12:14,799 --> 00:12:19,460
Also, again, it's just not visible in that classic establishing shot we keep looking at.

238
00:12:19,559 --> 00:12:21,940
So, what can we conclude about the Watterson's attic?

239
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:24,019
Well, it's in a pocket dimension, of course.

240
00:12:24,340 --> 00:12:25,320
Or maybe it's in the void.

241
00:12:25,559 --> 00:12:27,399
There's a whole lot of things that don't belong in there.

242
00:12:27,559 --> 00:12:30,059
Which brings me to the final room we'll be discussing.

243
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:33,379
Let's talk about the darkest room of the series, the basement.

244
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:37,899
You know, for the longest time, nobody in the house even knew this place had a basement,

245
00:12:38,059 --> 00:12:40,500
and who can blame them when this is how you access it?

246
00:12:40,679 --> 00:12:43,440
I don't really see how you can find a secret passage with that look.

247
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:47,200
And yeah, this place is as ominous as the steps down to it imply.

248
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:49,419
Look at how dark and creepy that is.

249
00:12:49,639 --> 00:12:50,720
Good golly, Goober.

250
00:12:50,740 --> 00:12:55,179
Yeah, the Watterson's have just never noticed this place as a creepy dungeon that can hide a bunch of stolen

251
00:12:55,179 --> 00:12:57,659
goods, or more importantly, hide stowaways.

252
00:13:02,779 --> 00:13:06,460
Yeah, this is the same room Rob hid in before going full-on evil.

253
00:13:06,620 --> 00:13:09,059
That kind of gives the basement a whole other level of creepiness.

254
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:13,200
It's a forgotten creepy, musty room that housed a poor kid who was forgotten about.

255
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:16,519
So forgotten about that he basically disappeared from existence entirely.

256
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:18,940
Even though Rob eventually left, I don't know.

257
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:21,100
I feel like that room's gotta be cursed now.

258
00:13:21,299 --> 00:13:23,740
I wouldn't want to live anywhere close to that place.

259
00:13:23,980 --> 00:13:27,879
Three, two, one, welcome to your new room, Darwin.

260
00:13:29,460 --> 00:13:30,299
Alright, I take it back.

261
00:13:30,399 --> 00:13:31,940
Honestly, they cleaned that place up nicely.

262
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:34,240
Darwin's a lucky fish to be able to call that place home.

263
00:13:34,419 --> 00:13:36,639
Though I can't get the feeling that this place still doesn't add up.

264
00:13:36,759 --> 00:13:38,220
Are we sure this place even exists?

265
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:41,539
Well, for no particular reason, let's watch this clip from the episode The Money,

266
00:13:41,659 --> 00:13:44,379
where the Watterson's become so broke that their house is taken away from them.

267
00:13:47,419 --> 00:13:51,080
You can't really take away a room built underground that easily.

268
00:13:51,299 --> 00:13:55,720
Also, I feel like if the basement did always truly exist, the family would've definitely noticed it here.

269
00:13:55,940 --> 00:14:00,700
You'd think they'd ask, hey, why is there a random scary passageway right underneath where our stairs were?

270
00:14:00,799 --> 00:14:02,200
But nope, nothing like that.

271
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:05,879
So, yet again, we got a room that disappears and reappears at whim.

272
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:08,789
Lovely. Although, again, maybe it's best this room disappeared.

273
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:13,080
I don't know if Rob left any void particles or anything that could wipe me out from existence down there,

274
00:14:13,159 --> 00:14:14,259
but I don't want to take any chances.

275
00:14:14,539 --> 00:14:17,799
But that's all I've got for y'all today, and if you want to see any more of the amazing,

276
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:22,159
wonderfully weird content on this channel, then click the video onscreen right about now.

277
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:24,379
Peace, guys, and as always, thank you for watching.

